{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 12.8% a year from FY2016 to FY2025, rising from $4,860.4m to $14,342.9m [F1][F10][F198]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was a step change, not a smooth compound: revenue jumped 89.1% in FY2021 to $16,071.7m [F6][D241], then fell 24.3% in FY2022 to $12,172.9m [F7][D292]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2021 spike came from REGEN-COV, whose U.S. sales of $5,828.0m contributed 66.4pp of that year's growth [S48][D582], and the FY2022 reversal followed as those sales fell to zero [S49][D585]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Since FY2022 revenue has grown only 5.6% a year to FY2025 [D767], and FY2025 growth was 1.0% [D440]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "In FY2025 net product sales fell 17.3%, subtracting 9.3pp from growth [D506][D507], while collaboration revenue rose 21.0% and added 9.0pp [D522][D523]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "U.S. EYLEA sales dropped 42.4% to $2,747.8m, a 14.2pp drag, on lower volumes from competitive pressure, compounded bevacizumab and the EYLEA HD transition, plus a lower net selling price [S43][D577][D578][P10]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "EYLEA HD partly offset that, rising 36.3% to $1,636.9m and adding 3.1pp, on higher volumes partly offset by a lower net selling price [S64][D613][D614][P11]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Regeneron's share of Sanofi antibody profits grew 33.6% to $5,241.6m, adding 9.3pp, driven by higher Dupixent sales [S52][D591][D592][P9]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating costs grew 4.4pp faster than revenue in FY2025, at 5.4% [D464][D457], and operating income fell 10.3% against 1.0% revenue growth [D441][D440]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin of 24.9% in FY2025 is the window low, 9.7pp below the 34.6% median and 30.8pp below the 55.7% FY2021 high [F30][D749][D751][D750]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2025 bridge was R&D -4.7pp, other lines -0.5pp, SG&A +2.0pp, for a net 3.2pp decline [D465][D467][D466][D453]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "R&D rose 14.0% to $5,850.2m, or 40.8% of revenue [X34][D455][D420], and SG&A fell 8.6% to $2,700.0m primarily on lower charitable contributions to Good Days [X47][D456][P5]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "In FY2025 net margin of 31.4% sat 6.5pp above the 24.9% operating margin [F50][F30], helped by $1,652.8m of other income [X117] and a 13.9% effective tax rate [D427]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $4,978.9m was 1.11x net income in FY2025 [F80][F40][D428], against a window median of 0.88x [D763]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow of $4,080.5m was a 28.4% margin [F100][D425], above the 26.4% window median [D757], with capex at 6.3% of revenue and 1.65x D&A [D424][D430]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Receivables fell 7.6% to $5,741.1m, lifting days sales outstanding to 146 [X197][D462][D438], while stock-based compensation of $993.7m was 20.0% of operating cash flow [X77][D431]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net cash of $16,879.9m equals 117.7% of revenue [D434][D435], in the 100th percentile of eight biopharma peers against a -50.7% median [D780][D781]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Debt is a flat $1,985.9m [F187][D461], and the current ratio of 4.13x sits above the 3.97x window median [F180][D766]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks and dividends of $3,808.9m consumed 93.3% of free cash flow in FY2025 [D436][D437], and the diluted share count fell 5.6% [D459]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "The balance sheet is the strongest part of the story, but the rising payout against free cash flow leaves less room if EYLEA erosion continues."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin has fallen four years running, from 55.7% in FY2021 to 24.9% in FY2025, a 30.7pp decline [F26][F30][R1]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "The decline is driven by EYLEA erosion and rising R&D intensity, so the margin low is a structural mix shift rather than a one-year cost spike."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "FY2018 and FY2019 revenue in the table is a later recast: $5,145.6m versus $6,710.8m first reported, and $6,557.6m versus $7,863.4m [F3][X3][F4][X4][R2]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "Growth and margins spanning those recast years mix two presentations, so the FY2018-FY2019 comparisons should not anchor a trend conclusion."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether U.S. EYLEA sales fall below the FY2025 level of $2,747.8m [S43] will confirm or reverse the product decline, in the FY2026 10-K."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether operating margin holds above the FY2025 window low of 24.9% [D749] will show if the four-year slide has stopped, in the FY2026 10-K."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether R&D stays above the FY2025 level of 40.8% of revenue [D420] against the 34.6% median [D760] will indicate whether reinvestment keeps pressuring margin, in the FY2026 10-K."}
  ]}
]}
